  "summary": "DIR-066 COMPLETE. (1) AUTOMATED THUMBNAIL REFRESH: template-lab/regenerate-previews.mjs already rendered all 51 previews from the real production path but hardcoded the Linux path /tmp/chromium-bin and required an EXTERNAL dev server. It now auto-detects the Playwright-bundled Chromium (CHROMIUM_PATH override, then LOCALAPPDATA/.cache ms-playwright chromium-*/chrome-win64|chrome-linux) and hosts vite IN-PROCESS (createServer on port 0 + warm-up) whenever LAB_BASE is unset, closing the server in a finally so no detached/background server can outlive the run (XAMPP invariant). Added an optional guarded sharp post-pass (dynamic import in try/catch) that strips metadata and re-encodes a baseline JPEG only when the result stays inside the 60KB-145KB gate and keeps its FFD8 magic. Ran it: all 51 of src/assets/resumesNew/Cv1.JPG..Cv51.JPG were regenerated from the current 10/10 engine, every one in-gate (86,561-122,490 bytes) and still a true A4 page-1 snapshot (993x1404, aspect 1.4139). (2) FRESHNESS PROOF: added template-lab/freshness-probe.mjs, a headless Playwright probe that re-renders each template live and compares a 16x16 grayscale signature of the live sheet against the stored CvN.JPG. Result: FRESHNESS PASS - all 51 thumbnails match the live adaptive engine (max mean-absolute-difference 5.92 against a 14 threshold), so the gallery provably reflects the modern 2-column card layouts. (3) CROSS-PORTAL PRINT/DOWNLOAD 10/10 VERIFICATION, all four surfaces confirmed wired: (A) Recruiter EmployerApplicantPipeline.jsx routes BOTH the isolated iframe print (createElement iframe + contentWindow.print) AND the HTML download (new Blob([buildPrintableDocument(...)])) through the shared print contract, so no chrome or skip-link bleed reaches paper; (B) Enterprise EnterpriseResumePdfModal.jsx uses window.print() and downloadResumeDocx from utils/exportDownloader; (C) User Dashboard DashboardHomepage.jsx uses downloadResumePdf + downloadResumeDocx from the centralized client; (D) Candidate BuildResume.jsx owns performDownload/performDocxDownload via the centralized client and hands PreviewModal onDownloadDocx plus onClick={onDownload}. (4) INTEGRITY GUARDS: zero OS console windows, no winget/cmd/PowerShell, no child_process/spawn/detached server in the refresh or probe; src/cv-templates git diff = 0; XAMPP policy guard 4/4. REGRESSION FIX: my new card builders briefly emitted an empty 'Projects' heading for whitespace-only content; restored the pre-existing guard using the canonical hasMeaningfulDocxText rule (handles <p> </p>, &nbsp;, and a lone U+200B zero-width space) so DOCX emptiness parity with the browser/PDF is preserved. EVIDENCE: new tests/dir066-thumbnail-and-portal-print.test.mjs 7/7 (51 thumbnails authentic/in-gate/A4-aspect/width>=900; refresh automated with no detached server; freshness probe fails closed; all four portals wired). DIR-064 + DIR-063 + template-previews + template-empty-sections 56/56; backend DOCX + DIR-065 + DIR-066 41/41; npm run test:templates 72/72 (includes the preview gate). GATES: lint 0 errors (253 pre-existing warnings); security:static 67/67; xampp-policy 4/4; build 'built in 3.05s' (under the 4.0s budget). HONEST LIMITS: the freshness probe proves the stored thumbnails match the live engine at 16x16 signature resolution (it is a staleness detector, not a pixel-exact diff); the thumbnails are captured with the canonical 'normal' fixture, so a template that only diverges under an extreme fixture would not be visible in its gallery card; the four portal checks are static wiring contracts plus the shared print/export primitives that already have browser coverage, not a fresh live authenticated click-through of each portal in this environment."
